(1333388, 168413, 14773, '<td valign="top">Seems by a comment or two as well as about half the entries, a lot of people thought you had to have rock, paper, AND scissors in this challenge. Not so! <br/> <br/>This shot finished well, but I honestly think it should''ve done better.</td>', 'Seems by a comment or two as well as about half the entries, a lot of people thought you had to have rock, paper, AND scissors in this challenge. Not so!  This shot finished well, but I honestly think it should''ve done better.', '2005-04-27 14:18:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1333654, 166921, 93, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the comments everyone!  24 is a great number to get for a 5.767 score.  I''m glad I could make people laugh with this, as I had a great time setting it up and coming up with the pun-like suicide note.<br/> <br/>A couple of thoughts:<br/>I wish I had the time or the tools to have drilled slots in the rocks for the scissors to fit in.. I would have been able to get a more "realistic" look.  <br/> <br/>Yes, I went over-board on the placement of the scissors, but I meant for this photo to be satirical, not life-like.. although, as I said above, a touch more "realism" might have helped.<br/> <br/>I explained the meaning of the note in my comments section, feel free to read that.<br/> <br/>Yes, this isn''t very technically inspiring, but I didn''t think it had to be.  The humor was all-important here, and if you didn''t get it, that''s ok.. I don''t fault you for that.   <br/> <br/>This is one of my personal favorite challenge entries.<br/>Once again, thank you to everyone.</td>', 'Thank you for the comments everyone!  24 is a great number to get for a 5.767 score.  I''m glad I could make people laugh with this, as I had a great time setting it up and coming up with the pun-like suicide note. A couple of thoughts:I wish I had the time or the tools to have drilled slots in the rocks for the scissors to fit in.. I would have been able to get a more "realistic" look.   Yes, I went over-board on the placement of the scissors, but I meant for this photo to be satirical, not life-like.. although, as I said above, a touch more "realism" might have helped. I explained the meaning of the note in my comments section, feel free to read that. Yes, this isn''t very technically inspiring, but I didn''t think it had to be.  The humor was all-important here, and if you didn''t get it, that''s ok.. I don''t fault you for that.    This is one of my personal favorite challenge entries.Once again, thank you to everyone.', '2005-04-27 15:00:04.000000', NULL, 0),
